# Favlo web-spa UI/UX

## Principle

Every change under `web-spa/` follows best UI/UX practice, and the result should be a pleasure to use. That is the rule. The sections after this one (tokens, contrast, buttons, surfaces, layout, motion) are how this repo meets it. They do not cap it. A change that passes every check below and still feels clumsy is not finished.

Best practice here means the published guidance this repo already leans on: [Material 3](https://m3.material.io/), Apple's [Human Interface Guidelines](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/), and [WCAG 2.2](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/) at AA. When a change makes a choice those sources address, follow them. Where the sources are silent or disagree, pick the option that serves the person using the screen, and say why in the change.

What a pleasure to use means in code:

- **The task is the subject.** Give the content the person came for the most room. Chrome stays quiet and gives way to it.
- **Nothing the person did goes away.** A scroll position, a half-typed message, a selection, a chosen size, and an open panel survive a resize, a rotation, the keyboard, and a trip to another view. Do not unmount a view to hide it when remounting loses that state.
- **Context stays in sight.** Do not make a person remember what they cannot see. Prefer one view that shows what belongs together over a switch between views. Prefer a non-modal surface over a modal one when the person is working with what is behind it. Use a modal for a choice that must be made first.
- **Every action answers.** A press, a send, a save, a failure, and a finished task each show a result the person can see, with no wait for the next screen. Loading, empty, error, and disabled states are designed, not left as blank space.
- **Motion has a cause.** Movement confirms a touch or explains a change in layout. It does not decorate. Honor reduced motion by cutting, not by removing the change.
- **Errors help.** Say what happened and what the person can do next, in plain words. Keep what they typed.
- **A narrow window is a first-class layout.** Reaching every control by thumb, targets of at least 44 points, no two-dimensional scrolling at 320 pixels, and a keyboard that never covers the box being typed into are part of done.
- **Keyboard and assistive technology work the same actions.** A control has a name, a role, a state, and a visible focus. Focus is never fully hidden behind docked content. A drag has a keyboard equivalent.
- **Destructive actions are asked once, said plainly, and kept distinct.** The confirmation names what is affected and what stays.

A choice between two options that work equally well takes the quieter one.

## Design system

Tokens live in `web-spa/src/theme/tokens.ts` (`light` / `dark` palettes, `space`, `radius`, `type`). Read the active palette with `useTheme()`. Paint text with `textStyle(role, palette.<token>)` from `web-spa/src/theme/type.ts`. Do not omit the color argument on visible text. Do not hardcode `#…`, `rgb(…)`, or theme-relative defaults on `Text`, icons, or buttons.

## Contrast

Body and UI text meet WCAG AA against the surface behind them. Prefer these pairs:

| Role | Token |
|---|---|
| Primary copy on `background` / `surface` | `palette.textPrimary` |
| Secondary / caption | `palette.textSecondary` |
| Links and ghost controls | `palette.accent` |
| Errors / destructive labels | `palette.danger` |
| Disabled label | `palette.disabledText` on `palette.disabledSurface` |

Nested `Text` (markdown strong, em, code, links, and other inline roles) sets its own `color`; it does not inherit a parent RN-web style. Omitting color leaves browser defaults that fail on dark surfaces.

## Buttons

`IconButton` takes either `tone` or an explicit `background` + `color` paint. Prefer `tone` so pairs stay correct:

| Tone | Fill | Label / icon |
|---|---|---|
| `accent` | `palette.accent` | `palette.onAccent` |
| `danger` | `palette.danger` | `palette.onDanger` |
| `surface` | `palette.surface` | `palette.textPrimary` (border `borderStrong`) |
| `ghost` | transparent | `palette.accent` |
| `dangerGhost` | transparent | `palette.danger` |

`buttonPaint(palette, tone)` in `web-spa/src/theme/buttons.ts` is the single map. Wrong: `background={palette.danger}` with `color={palette.onAccent}` or with no color. Wrong: an `IconButton` with neither `tone` nor `background`/`color`. Disabled controls use `disabledSurface` / `disabledText`, not a muted accent.

## Surfaces

Page chrome uses `palette.background`. Cards, drawers, and dialogs use `palette.surface` or `palette.surfaceRaised`. Borders use `palette.border` or `palette.borderStrong`. Focus rings use `palette.focusRing` (see `Pressable`). Overlays use `palette.overlay`.

## Layout (react-native-web)

Do not mix the `flex` shorthand with `flexGrow`, `flexShrink`, or `flexBasis` on the same style object, and do not toggle `flex` to `undefined` across renders while those longhands stay set. RN-web warns and can leave stale CSS. Prefer longhands when any one of them varies (`flexGrow` / `flexShrink` / `flexBasis`).

## Motion

Keep ambient activity quiet. Prefer opacity (and tiny scale) pulses with `ease-in-out` over traveling high-contrast light on text. Cycles for “still working” feedback should land around 2–2.5s, not under ~1.5s with `linear`. Do not clip label text with a shimmer gradient that flashes to `onAccent` or white. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` by freezing decorative loops. The Working chip uses `workingActivity` in `web-spa/src/components/working.ts`.

## Checklist before finishing a SPA change

- The person can see the result of every action they can start, in the state it leaves behind.
- A view or panel hidden by a switch keeps its scroll position, draft, and selection.
- On a narrow window, the content, the control that completes the task, and the context it depends on are on screen together, or the way between them is one obvious control.
- Loading, empty, and error states exist for anything fetched or generated.
- Every target is at least 44 points. A drag has a keyboard path. Focus is visible and not hidden by docked content.
- Every new `Text` passes a palette color into `textStyle`.
- Every `IconButton` / filled control uses `tone` or a documented paint pair.
- No new raw hex in component files (tokens only).
- Dark and light both stay readable; if unsure, check `contrast()` in `tokens.ts` (AA ≥ 4.5 for small text).
- No `flex` shorthand mixed with `flexGrow` / `flexShrink` / `flexBasis`.
- New ambient loops follow Motion above and respect reduced motion.
- New movement has a cause the person can see, and reduced motion turns it into a cut.
- The change reads as a pleasure to use on a phone-sized window and on a desktop window. When it does not, it is not finished, even if each check above passes.
